---
import Layout from '../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { sitePath } from '../../../lib/siteUrl';
---

<Layout title="Image Enhance — Varve Docs" description="Use Varve's local-first image enhancement workflow for denoising and upscaling.">
  <div class="container-custom">
    <article class="docs-page">
      <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href={sitePath('/docs')}>Documentation</a> / Tools / Image Enhance</nav>
      <h1>Image Enhance</h1>
      <p class="docs-intro">Clean up and enlarge a selected image without leaving the canvas.</p>

      <section class="docs-section">
        <h2>Choose the task</h2>
        <p>Open the existing image enhancement command for a selected image and choose the operation that matches the source problem:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Denoise</strong> reduces sensor noise and grain using Varve's task-specific local denoising path.</li>
          <li><strong>Upscale</strong> enlarges with CPU, pixel-art, or the available local AI super-resolution path.</li>
          <li><strong>Restore + Upscale</strong> composes denoising before enlargement.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="docs-section">
        <h2>Review before applying</h2>
        <p>The dialog previews a bounded representative crop and provides a draggable before/after comparison. Use the preview at a useful zoom for text, logos, thin lines, transparency, and edge transitions. A preview is not a full-resolution final result.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="docs-section">
        <h2>Output behavior</h2>
        <p><strong>New layer</strong> is the default and preserves the source. <strong>Replace source</strong> commits the derived pixels atomically and remains undoable. Use the output options only when their semantics suit the document; enhancement results are materialized pixels and do not silently become re-editable model operations.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="docs-section docs-note">
        <h2>Honest capabilities</h2>
        <p>Deblur and JPEG artifact removal are not currently presented as available operations without task-specific model validation. Varve does not relabel a denoiser as a deblurring or compression-restoration model, and it does not substitute an unrelated fallback when a requested task cannot run.</p>
      </section>
    </article>
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  .docs-page { max-width: 800px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 3rem 0 5rem; }
  .breadcrumb { color: var(--text-secondary); font-size: .875rem; margin-bottom: 1.5rem; }
  .breadcrumb a { color: var(--text-secondary); }
  h1 { color: var(--text-primary); font: 700 clamp(2rem, 5vw, 2.8rem)/1.1 var(--font-editorial); margin-bottom: 1rem; }
  .docs-intro { color: var(--text-secondary); font-size: 1.15rem; margin-bottom: 3rem; }
  .docs-section { margin-bottom: 2.5rem; }
  .docs-section h2 { border-bottom: 2px solid var(--border-accent); color: var(--text-primary); font-size: 1.45rem; margin-bottom: 1rem; padding-bottom: .5rem; }
  .docs-section p, .docs-section li { color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.8; }
  .docs-section li { margin-bottom: .5rem; }
  .docs-note { border-left: 3px solid var(--accent-primary); padding-left: 1rem; }
</style>
